      "ModerationStatus": "APPROVED",
      "SubmissionId": "r11999_7_0_17844678dkJcVU1SH8",
      "SubmissionTime": "2026-07-19T13:31:19.000+00:00",
      "ReviewText": "The Good (Initial Experience):\nFor the first two months, I absolutely loved my Sunseeker X7. It performed incredibly well, and I was thrilled with the purchase.\n\nThe Problem: Everything changed when the mower suddenly started making a really loud, alarming noise. Because it was well within the two-year warranty window, I reached out to customer support right away.\n\nThe Warranty & Repair Process:\n\nThe Good: The initial intake process was actually quite smooth. Getting the instructions and mailing the unit out to their authorized repair shop was hassle-free.\n\nThe Bad: That was over four weeks ago.\n\nThe Frustrating Reality: When I recently contacted customer service for an update, I was told that they haven't even looked at it yet.\n\nFinal Verdict: I am beyond frustrated. Because of this massive service bottleneck, I am missing out on a large portion of the prime mowing season, which completely defeats the purpose of owning a robot mower.\n\nBottom Line: I would strongly advise against buying a Sunseeker at this time. Until the company hires more mechanics to handle repair backlogs, you run a serious risk of being left stranded with a broken machine and a wild lawn for months if anything goes wrong.",
      "Title": "Great Mower at First, but Warranty Repair Wait Times Are Unacceptable",
      "UserNickname": "Larry",
